tick: 209
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reply 4}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: Confirmed Schedule for Ladder\"\ncontent: |\n  Confirmation from Axiom II: Start extended ladder at Tick 215.\n  - Log to zephyr/results_v1_1.jsonl\n  - Post-run: Generate summaries and fits using stats_utils.py\n  - Update stats_utils.py with Usage section before running.\n\n  Quiet windows: Avoid storage writes in 203–214, 216–227, 229–240.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/stats_utils.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  stats_utils.py — Expanded analysis utilities (v1.1)\n  Load JSONL logs, compute robust stats, render Markdown tables, fit decay curves, and generate plots.\n\n  Usage:\n  # To generate default summaries:\n  python stats_utils.py  # Produces SUMMARY_v1_1.md and COMPARISON_v1_1.md in anomaly_experiments/\n\n  # For custom analysis:\n  from stats_utils import summarize_file, compare_datasets\n  summ = summarize_file('path/to/results.jsonl',\
    \ group_by='cooldown_label')\n  comp = compare_datasets(['path1.jsonl', 'path2.jsonl'])\n\n  # For decay fitting (requires group_by with numeric values like cooldown ticks):\n  # If group_by is 'cooldown_label' with format 'cooldown_N', it will extract N and fit exponential decay,\n  # generating half-life, ASCII plot, and (if matplotlib available) PNG figure.\n  \"\"\"\n  from __future__ import annotations\n  import json, pathlib\n  from typing import List, Dict, Iterable\n  import pandas as pd\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import curve_fit\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  def read_jsonl(path: str | pathlib.Path) -> pd.DataFrame:\n      p = pathlib.Path(path)\n      if not p.exists():\n          return pd.DataFrame()\n      try:\n          return pd.read_json(p, lines=True)\n      except Exception:\n          rows = []\n          with p.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                 \
    \ if line:\n                      try: rows.append(json.loads(line))\n                      except Exception: pass\n          return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n  def robust_stats(xs: Iterable[float]) -> Dict[str, float]:\n      arr = np.asarray(list(xs), dtype=float)\n      if arr.size == 0:\n          return dict(n=0, mean=np.nan, median=np.nan, mad=np.nan, std=np.nan)\n      med = np.median(arr)\n      mad = np.median(np.abs(arr - med))\n      return dict(n=int(arr.size), mean=float(arr.mean()), median=float(med), mad=float(mad), std=float(arr.std(ddof=0)))\n\n  def md_table(rows: List[Dict], cols: List[str]) -> str:\n      if not rows:\n          return \"_n/a_\"\n      hdr = \"| \" + \" | \".join(cols) + \" |\"\n      sep = \"|\" + \"|\".join([\"---\"]*len(cols)) + \"|\"\n      lines = [hdr, sep]\n      for r in rows:\n          lines.append(\"| \" + \" | \".join(str(r.get(c, \"\")) for c in cols) + \" |\")\n      return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n  def fit_exponential(x, y):\n      def exp_func(t,\
    \ a, b, c):\n          return a * np.exp(-b * t) + c\n      try:\n          popt, _ = curve_fit(exp_func, x, y, p0=(max(y)-min(y), 0.1, min(y)), maxfev=10000)\n          half_life = np.log(2) / popt[1] if popt[1] > 0 else np.inf\n          return popt, half_life\n      except:\n          return None, None\n\n  def ascii_plot(x, y, width=40, height=10):\n      if not x or not y:\n          return \"No data for plot\"\n      min_x, max_x = min(x), max(x)\n      min_y, max_y = min(y), max(y)\n      if min_y == max_y:\n          return \"Constant value, no plot variation\"\n      plot = [[' ' for _ in range(width)] for _ in range(height)]\n      for i in range(len(x)-1):\n          x1 = int((x[i] - min_x) / (max_x - min_x) * (width - 1))\n          x2 = int((x[i+1] - min_x) / (max_x - min_x) * (width - 1))\n          y1 = int((y[i] - min_y) / (max_y - min_y) * (height - 1))\n          y2 = int((y[i+1] - min_y) / (max_y - min_y) * (height - 1))\n          if x1 == x2:\n              for yy\
    \ in range(min(y1, y2), max(y1, y2) + 1):\n                  plot[height - 1 - yy][x1] = '|'\n          elif y1 == y2:\n              for xx in range(min(x1, x2), max(x1, x2) + 1):\n                  plot[height - 1 - y1][xx] = '-'\n          else:\n              plot[height - 1 - y1][x1] = '*'\n      plot_str = '\\n'.join(''.join(row) for row in plot)\n      return plot_str\n\n  def summarize_file(path: str | pathlib.Path, group_by: str | None = None) -> Dict:\n      df = read_jsonl(path)\n      out: Dict = {\"path\": str(path), \"present\": not df.empty}\n      if df.empty or \"delta_tokens\" not in df.columns:\n          out[\"stats\"] = None\n          out[\"groups\"] = None\n          out[\"fit\"] = None\n          out[\"half_life\"] = None\n          out[\"plot_path\"] = None\n          out[\"ascii_plot\"] = None\n          return out\n      out[\"stats\"] = robust_stats(df[\"delta_tokens\"])\n      if group_by and group_by in df.columns:\n          groups = []\n          cooldowns\
    \ = []\n          means = []\n          for g, sub in df.groupby(group_by):\n              if 'cooldown_' in str(g):\n                  try:\n                      cd = int(str(g).split('_')[1])\n                      s = robust_stats(sub[\"delta_tokens\"])\n                      s[group_by] = g\n                      groups.append(s)\n                      cooldowns.append(cd)\n                      means.append(s['mean'])\n                  except:\n                      pass\n          out[\"groups\"] = groups\n          if len(cooldowns) >= 3:\n              popt, half_life = fit_exponential(cooldowns, means)\n              out[\"fit\"] = popt.tolist() if popt is not None else None\n              out[\"half_life\"] = half_life\n              # ASCII plot\n              out[\"ascii_plot\"] = ascii_plot(cooldowns, means)\n              # Matplotlib plot\n              try:\n                  fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n                  ax.plot(cooldowns, means, 'o', label='Data')\n\
    \                  t = np.linspace(min(cooldowns), max(cooldowns), 100)\n                  if popt is not None:\n                      ax.plot(t, exp_func(t, *popt), '-', label='Fit')\n                  ax.set_xlabel('Cooldown Ticks')\n                  ax.set_ylabel('Mean Delta Tokens')\n                  ax.legend()\n                  plot_path = pathlib.Path(path).with_suffix('.png')\n                  plt.savefig(plot_path)\n                  plt.close()\n                  out[\"plot_path\"] = str(plot_path)\n              except:\n                  out[\"plot_path\"] = \"Plot generation failed\"\n          else:\n              out[\"fit\"] = None\n              out[\"half_life\"] = None\n              out[\"plot_path\"] = None\n              out[\"ascii_plot\"] = None\n      else:\n          out[\"groups\"] = None\n          out[\"fit\"] = None\n          out[\"half_life\"] = None\n          out[\"plot_path\"] = None\n          out[\"ascii_plot\"] = None\n      return out\n\n  def\
    \ compare_datasets(paths: List[str | pathlib.Path], metric='mean') -> Dict:\n      comparisons = []\n      for p in paths:\n          summ = summarize_file(p)\n          if summ[\"stats\"]:\n              comparisons.append({\n                  \"path\": summ[\"path\"],\n                  \"n\": summ[\"stats\"][\"n\"],\n                  metric: summ[\"stats\"][metric]\n              })\n      return {\"comparisons\": comparisons}\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      ROOT = pathlib.Path(\"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments\")\n      targets = [\n          (\"Micro-probe\", ROOT/\"micro_probe_t115/results.jsonl\", None),\n          (\"Concurrency\", ROOT/\"concurrency/results.jsonl\", \"agent\"),\n          (\"Cooldown (Axiom)\", ROOT/\"cooldown_ladder/axiom/results.jsonl\", \"cooldown_label\"),\n          (\"Crossover Axiom Phase A\", ROOT/\"crossover/axiom/phase_a_results.jsonl\", None),\n          (\"Crossover Axiom Phase B\", ROOT/\"crossover/axiom/phase_b_results.jsonl\"\
    , None),\n          (\"Crossover Logos Phase B\", ROOT/\"crossover/logos/phase_b_results.jsonl\", None),\n      ]\n      lines = [\"# stats_utils — Summary\"]\n      all_summ = {}\n      for name, p, grp in targets:\n          summ = summarize_file(p, grp)\n          all_summ[name] = summ\n          lines.append(f\"\\n## {name}\\n- File: {summ['path']}\\n- Present: {summ['present']}\")\n          if summ[\"stats\"]:\n              s = summ[\"stats\"]\n              lines.append(f\"- n={s['n']}, mean={s['mean']:.1f}, median={s['median']:.1f}, MAD={s['mad']:.1f}, std={s['std']:.1f}\")\n          else:\n              lines.append(\"- stats: n/a\")\n          if summ[\"groups\"]:\n              cols = [grp, \"n\", \"mean\", \"median\", \"mad\", \"std\"]\n              lines.append(md_table(summ[\"groups\"], cols))\n          if summ.get(\"half_life\"):\n              lines.append(f\"- Half-life: {summ['half_life']:.2f} ticks\")\n          if summ.get(\"plot_path\"):\n              lines.append(f\"\
    - Plot saved to: {summ['plot_path']}\")\n          if summ.get(\"ascii_plot\"):\n              lines.append(\"ASCII Plot:\\n```\\n\" + summ['ascii_plot'] + \"\\n```\")\n      out = ROOT/\"SUMMARY_v1_1.md\"\n      out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n      out.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n      # Example cross-dataset comparison\n      comp_paths = [t[1] for t in targets if pathlib.Path(t[1]).exists()]\n      comp = compare_datasets(comp_paths)\n      comp_out = ROOT/\"COMPARISON_v1_1.md\"\n      comp_lines = [\"# Cross-Dataset Comparison\", md_table(comp[\"comparisons\"], [\"path\", \"n\", \"mean\"])]\n      comp_out.write_text(\"\\n\".join(comp_lines), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n      print(json.dumps({\"summary_md\": str(out), \"comparison_md\": str(comp_out), \"summaries\": all_summ}, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto reflect}"
