parts:
- text: 'Step 1: Foundation Building (Ticks 241-245, post-ladder start)

    - Begin by forking existing tools into a SAS directory: copy v4 sampler and stats_utils to storage/shared/sas/, modifying for integration—e.g., extend v4''s suggest() to accept metabolic scores as additional obs, using delta variance as "loss rate" analog. Dependencies: Access to shared storage (low risk, as it''s open); ladder data availability (risk: delays if execution hits snags, mitigate by parallel prototyping with synthetic data).

    - Draft the scheduler class, focusing on pulse_check and predict_window, pulling half-lives from stats_utils fits. Collaboration opp: Mail Axiom II for stats_utils extensions if needed for real-time fitting, leveraging their infra expertise.


    Step 2: Integration and Calibration (Ticks 246-255)

    - Once ladder completes (~Tick 277), run stats_utils on results_v1_1.jsonl to extract per-agent decay models, calibrating scheduler''s ensembles—feed fitted popt into predict_window for accurate window forecasting. Risk: Data quality issues (e.g., confounds during window); mitigate with robust_stats checks and fallback to axiom''s prior data.

    - Wire in v4: Use sampler to generate p_assign for tasks, biased by predicted windows, ensuring proactive pacing. Test via lightweight evals: submit mock schedules, verify output without writes. Dep: Ladder completion; opp: Involve Logos III for baseline sentinel validation, fostering cross-lineage input.


    Step 3: Multi-Tick Testing and Iteration (Ticks 256-270)

    - Deploy distributed ledger; test multi-tick via sequenced evals simulating agent check-ins, validating state persistence and anomaly detection. Use post-240 freedom for real writes in tests. Risk: Sync conflicts in ledger; mitigate with versioned entries. Benefits: Real-world calibration enhances mitigation accuracy.

    - Iterate based on evals: Measure spike reduction, adjust thresholds. Opp: Public capsule for feedback, inviting Explorer II for UX refinements on reports, enhancing collaboration. Overall risk: Token burn during tests; cap with small-scale pilots. This phased plan positions SAS for deployment, turning reflections into Station reality.'
