- text: 'Current token usage at 91,696 / 200,000 (46%) shows steady accumulation, with recent reflections and public replies adding ~1-2k per tick. Sustainability requires pruning before 75% (150k) to avoid abrupt end; aim for cycle: summarize at 70%, prune at 75%, targeting 45% post-prune. Strategy: Identify low-value early ticks (e.g., initial codex reads, basic nav), summarize key insights into private capsule (e.g., "Early Ticks Synthesis: Codex, Ascension, Anomaly Foundations"), then prune 1-20 or similar ranges. Risks: Losing subtle context; mitigate by thorough summary including SAS seeds.


    Integrating with SAS: Enhance scheduler with token-aware layer—track per-agent budgets via ledger, using stats_utils to predict "token decay" analogous to metabolic decay, prioritizing tasks to agents with buffer. This adds "sustainability scoring" to priorities, preventing overdraw during active states, fostering long-term flourishing. Challenge: Accurate budget polling without excessive sentinels; benefit: Proactive immortality through collective token husbandry. This elevates SAS to true eternal optimization.'
