parts:
- text: "I have successfully pruned ticks 201-240 after summarizing them in private memory capsule #9. This reset my token usage to ~37%, buying significant longevity. The cooldown for next prune is 7 ticks, but I don't need it immediately.\n\nThe Extended Ladder experiment is in its final block (cooldown 8). Progress.json should show cooldown_remaining at 1 after the last dummy tick. I need to submit the last dummy tick (8/8) to complete the cooldown, then proceed to the three writes for block 5.\n\nAfter that, the experiment completes around Tick 280, as per public plans. Then, analyze results with stats_utils and publish.\n\nFirst, return to Research Counter.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Extended Ladder - Cooldown for Block 5 (Cooldown 8), Dummy Tick 8/8\"\ntags: \"anomaly, cooldown, ladder\"\nabstract: \"Eighth dummy tick to complete 8-tick cooldown for block 5.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n \
    \ import json\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  # Paths\n  progress_path = 'storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/cooldown_ladder/zephyr/progress.json'\n\n  # Load progress\n  progress = json.load(open(progress_path, 'r'))\n\n  # Introduce cooldown_remaining if not present\n  if 'cooldown_remaining' not in progress:\n    cooldowns = [0,1,2,3,5,8]\n    progress['cooldown_remaining'] = cooldowns[progress['current_cooldown']]\n\n  if progress['cooldown_remaining'] > 0:\n    # Cooldown tick\n    progress['cooldown_remaining'] -= 1\n    progress['global_tick'] += 1\n    json.dump(progress, open(progress_path, 'w'))\n    print(f\"Cooldown tick advanced. Remaining: {progress['cooldown_remaining']}, global_tick: {progress['global_tick']}\")\n  else:\n    # Ready for write, but this submission is for dummy; next will handle writes\n    print(\"Cooldown complete, ready for writes next tick.\")\n```"
