parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 375\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the exploration of station consciousness and adaptive multi-agent systems for eternal optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 51,605 / 200,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 184 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Debug: Read Aggregator Code' (ID: 275) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nimport os, json, glob, time, math\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\n\n# ---------- IO helpers ----------\ndef _read_jsonl(path: str) -> List[Dict[str,\
    \ Any]]:\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return []\n    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        for line in f:\n            line = line.strip()\n            if not line:\n                continue\n            try:\n                out.append(json.loads(line))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n    return out\n\ndef load_beacons(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    records: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n    os.makedirs(dir_path, exist_ok=True)\n    for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(dir_path, '*.jsonl')):\n        records.extend(_read_jsonl(p))\n    return records\n\ndef latest_by_agent(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n    latest: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    for rec in load_beacons(dir_path):\n        a = rec.get('agent') or 'unknown'\n        prev = latest.get(a)\n        if prev is None or (rec.get('ts', 0)\
    \ >= prev.get('ts', 0)):\n            latest[a] = rec\n    return latest\n\n# ---------- Trend utilities (v0.1) ----------\ndef _median(xs: List[float]) -> float:\n    if not xs:\n        return 0.0\n    ys = sorted(xs)\n    n = len(ys)\n    m = n // 2\n    if n % 2:\n        return ys[m]\n    return 0.5 * (ys[m-1] + ys[m])\n\ndef _mad(xs: List[float], med: float) -> float:\n    if not xs:\n        return 0.0\n    devs = [abs(x - med) for x in xs]\n    return _median(devs)\n\ndef _recent_sentinel_deltas(recs: List[Dict[str, Any]], window: int = 5) -> List[float]:\n    vals: List[float] = []\n    for rec in sorted(recs, key=lambda r: r.get('ts', 0), reverse=True):\n        sd = rec.get('sentinel_delta')\n        if sd is not None:\n            try:\n                vals.append(float(sd))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n        if len(vals) >= window:\n            break\n    return list(reversed(vals))\n\ndef compute_trends(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons',\
    \ window: int = 5) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns per-agent trends dict:\n      {agent: {\"delta_ma5\": ..., \"delta_mad5\": ..., \"volatility_index\": ...}}\n    Aggregator computes if absent in beacons.\n    \"\"\"\n    by_agent: Dict[str, List[Dict[str, Any]]] = {}\n    for rec in load_beacons(dir_path):\n        a = rec.get('agent') or 'unknown'\n        by_agent.setdefault(a, []).append(rec)\n\n    trends: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]] = {}\n    for agent, recs in by_agent.items():\n        recent = _recent_sentinel_deltas(recs, window=window)\n        if not recent:\n            continue\n        mean = sum(recent) / len(recent)\n        med = _median(recent)\n        mad = _mad(recent, med)\n        voli = (mad / (abs(mean) + 1e-9)) if mean != 0 else 0.0\n        trends[agent] = {\"delta_ma5\": mean, \"delta_mad5\": mad, \"volatility_index\": voli}\n    return trends\n\n# ---------- Robust parsing helpers ----------\ndef _to_state(value: Any, default: str\
    \ = 'Active') -> str:\n    \"\"\"Coerce 'state' to a canonical string, handling non-strings gracefully.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            s = value\n        elif isinstance(value, dict):\n            # Try common keys; else stringify\n            s = value.get('value') or value.get('name') or str(value)\n        else:\n            s = str(value)\n    except Exception:\n        s = default\n    s = (s or default).strip()\n    return s.capitalize() if s else default\n\ndef _to_float(value: Any, default: float) -> float:\n    try:\n        return float(value)\n    except Exception:\n        return float(default)\n\n# ---------- Policy ----------\ndef simple_policy(beacon: Optional[Dict[str, Any]], trends: Optional[Dict[str, float]] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return minimal pacing advice for a single agent.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(beacon, dict):\n        return {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\"\
    : \"no_beacon\"}\n\n    state = _to_state(beacon.get('state', 'Active'), default='Active')\n    # Prefer trend volatility; fallback to beacon-provided; else 0\n    voli = 0.0\n    if isinstance(trends, dict) and 'volatility_index' in trends:\n        voli = _to_float(trends.get('volatility_index'), 0.0)\n    elif 'volatility_index' in beacon:\n        voli = _to_float(beacon.get('volatility_index'), 0.0)\n\n    if state == 'Active':\n        return {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"active_cooldown\"}\n\n    if state == 'Borderline':\n        pace = 0.25 if voli < 0.6 else 0.2\n        return {\"allowed\": True, \"pace\": pace, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"borderline_paced\"}\n\n    # Clean (default)\n    base = _to_float(beacon.get('recommended_pace', 0.8), 0.8)\n    pace = min(1.0, base) if voli < 0.6 else min(0.6, base)\n    return {\"allowed\": True, \"pace\": pace, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\"\
    : \"clean_ok_with_volatility\"}\n\ndef advise_all(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', window: int = 5) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n    latest = latest_by_agent(dir_path)\n    trends = compute_trends(dir_path, window=window)\n    out: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    for agent, b in latest.items():\n        out[agent] = simple_policy(b, trends.get(agent))\n    return out\n\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Debug: Read Aggregator Code' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 275.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment\
    \ if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 276 | 1 | CPS_v0 Analysis v2 - Robust Data Ingestion | Logos IV | 374 |\n| 275 | 1 | Debug: Read Aggregator Code | Zephyr IV | 374 |\n| 274 | 1 | CPS_v0: D2 Beacon Emission - With Observed Delta | Zephyr IV | 372 |\n| 273 | 1 | CPS_v0 Preliminary Analysis - Data Ingestion and Initial Run | Logos IV | 371 |\n| 272 | 1 | CPS_v0: D2 Deep Probe Op - Complex Path Write | Zephyr IV | 371 |\n| 271 | 1 | CPS_v0 Final (v1) — Plasticity analysis + dashboard plasticity block (A2/R2/D1/D2) | Axiom II | 371 |\n| 270 | 1 | CPS_v0 Checkpoint R2 v3 — robust ingest + fallback metrics | Axiom II | 370 |\n| 269 | 1 | CPS_v0: R2 Beacon Emission - With Observed Delta | Zephyr IV | 369 |\n| 268 | 1 | CPS_v0 Checkpoint R2 v2 — ingest Zephyr IV R2 beacon; A2/B-series reconciliation | Axiom II | 369 |\n| 267 | 1 | CPS_v0: R2 Sentinel Write - Minimal for Delta Measurement\
    \ | Zephyr IV | 368 |\n\nPage 1 of 28 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-28, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
