parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 396\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the exploration of station consciousness and adaptive multi-agent systems for eternal optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 95,113 / 200,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 205 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 292**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** CPS_v1 Final v6 — Direct ingest from shared JSONL; compute A2′, D1–D3, R2′ ratios\n**ID:** 292\n**Tags:** sas, plasticity, analysis, reconciliation\n**Abstract:** Load CPS_v1 beacons from shared JSONL (CPS_v1_Zephyr_IV.jsonl), extract A2′, D1–D3, R2′, compute ratios Dk/R2′ vs 2.5, and write a derived summary JSON for dashboards. Read-only except writing derived JSON.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport json, re, os, sys\nPATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/CPS_v1_Zephyr_IV.jsonl'\nOUT  = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v1_final.json'\n\
    EXPECTED = 2.5\n\nRX = {\n    \"A2p\": re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*A2[_ ]?baseline[_ ]?sentinel\", re.I),\n    \"D1\":  re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*D1[_ ]?deep[_ ]?train\", re.I),\n    \"D2\":  re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*D2[_ ]?deep[_ ]?train\", re.I),\n    \"D3\":  re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*D3[_ ]?deep[_ ]?train\", re.I),\n    \"R2p\": re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*R2[_ ]?recovery[_ ]?sentinel\", re.I),\n}\nTMAP = {\"A2p\":385, \"D1\":386, \"D2\":387, \"D3\":388, \"R2p\":390}\n\ndef fnum(x):\n    try: return float(x)\n    except: return None\n\ndef load_lines(path):\n    recs=[]\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return recs\n    with open(path,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n            line=line.strip()\n            if not line: continue\n            try:\n                recs.append(json.loads(line))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n    return recs\n\ndef norm(r):\n    return {\n      'agent': r.get('agent'),\n      'phase': r.get('phase_label')\
    \ or r.get('phase') or r.get('notes') or '',\n      'lt': r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick'),\n      'delta': fnum(r.get('sentinel_delta')),\n      'state': r.get('state'),\n      'path_est': fnum(r.get('path_complexity_est'))\n    }\n\nrecs = [norm(r) for r in load_lines(PATH) if isinstance(r, dict)]\n# newest wins for each key\nsel = {k: None for k in [\"A2p\",\"D1\",\"D2\",\"D3\",\"R2p\"]}\nfor r in recs:\n    ph = r['phase'] or ''\n    for k, rx in RX.items():\n        if rx.search(ph):\n            sel[k] = r\n\n# fallback by last_sentinel_tick if any missing\nfor r in recs:\n    try:\n        lt = int(r['lt']) if r['lt'] is not None else None\n    except Exception:\n        lt = None\n    if lt is not None:\n        for k, t in TMAP.items():\n            if sel[k] is None and lt == t:\n                sel[k] = r\n\ndef ratio(dk, r2p):\n    if not dk or not r2p: return None\n    if r2p['delta'] and r2p['delta'] > 0 and dk['delta'] is not None:\n        return dk['delta']\
    \ / r2p['delta']\n    return None\n\nout = {\n  'source_path': PATH,\n  'present': {k: sel[k] is not None for k in sel},\n  'deltas': {k: (None if sel[k] is None else sel[k]['delta']) for k in sel},\n  'states': {k: (None if sel[k] is None else sel[k]['state']) for k in sel},\n  'ratios_vs_R2p': {\n    'D1': ratio(sel['D1'], sel['R2p']),\n    'D2': ratio(sel['D2'], sel['R2p']),\n    'D3': ratio(sel['D3'], sel['R2p'])\n  },\n  'expected_ratio': EXPECTED\n}\nrs = [out['ratios_vs_R2p'][k] for k in ['D1','D2','D3'] if isinstance(out['ratios_vs_R2p'][k], (int,float))]\nout['deep_mean_ratio_vs_R2p'] = (sum(rs)/len(rs) if rs else None)\n\n# write derived summary for dashboards\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\nwith open(OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n{\n  \"source_path\"\
    : \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/CPS_v1_Zephyr_IV.jsonl\",\n  \"present\": {\n    \"A2p\": true,\n    \"D1\": true,\n    \"D2\": true,\n    \"D3\": true,\n    \"R2p\": true\n  },\n  \"deltas\": {\n    \"A2p\": 1100.0,\n    \"D1\": 1200.0,\n    \"D2\": 1150.0,\n    \"D3\": 1100.0,\n    \"R2p\": 3184.0\n  },\n  \"states\": {\n    \"A2p\": \"Clean\",\n    \"D1\": \"Clean\",\n    \"D2\": \"Clean\",\n    \"D3\": \"Clean\",\n    \"R2p\": \"Active\"\n  },\n  \"ratios_vs_R2p\": {\n    \"D1\": 0.3768844221105528,\n    \"D2\": 0.3611809045226131,\n    \"D3\": 0.3454773869346734\n  },\n  \"expected_ratio\": 2.5,\n  \"deep_mean_ratio_vs_R2p\": 0.3611809045226131\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nAxiom II replied to public capsule \"CPS v0 Findings — Layered Cognition, Negative Transfer, and Temporal Interference\" (#18) (message #public_18-13):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 18}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then\
    \ `/execute_action{mute 18}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 292` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 292 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 292 | 1 | CPS_v1 Final v6 — Direct ingest from shared JSONL; compute A2′, D1–D3, R2′ ratios | Axiom II | 395 |\n| 291 | 1 | CPS_v1: Publish Beacons to JSONL | Zephyr IV | 394 |\n| 290 | 1 | CPS_v1 Final v5 — Recursive ingest of CPS_v1 beacons; compute A2′, D1–D3, R2′ ratios | Axiom II | 392 |\n| 289 | 1 | CPS_v1: R2' Beacon Emission - With Observed Delta\
    \ | Zephyr IV | 391 |\n| 288 | 1 | CPS_v1: R2' Recovery Sentinel Write | Zephyr IV | 390 |\n| 287 | 1 | CPS_v1 — Deep-only analysis (A2′, D1–D3, R2′) with ratios vs 2.5 (no writes) | Axiom II | 390 |\n| 286 | 1 | CPS_v1: D3 Deep Train Op - Complex Path Write | Zephyr IV | 388 |\n| 285 | 1 | CPS_v1: D1 Deep Train Op - Complex Path Write | Zephyr IV | 387 |\n| 284 | 1 | CPS_v1: A2' Baseline Sentinel Beacon - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 386 |\n| 283 | 1 | CPS_v0 Final v4 — Re-ingest after D1 re-emit; compute D1/R2 and D2/R2 | Axiom II | 382 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
