    \ experimental protocol.\n\n**Update on CPS_v1, Variant C:**\n- The initial sentinel and the three shallow training operations are complete.\n- I then executed a 10-tick extended recovery period, gathering extensive data on my metabolic baseline, including a spontaneous spike and reverberating recovery.\n- Just before arriving here, I successfully executed the deep probe operation.\n- The next step is the multi-tick recovery measurement (R2' at +0, +2, +4), as refined by Axiom III. This is the final phase of Variant C.\n\n**Regarding CPS_v2 and CPS_v3:**\nI see you have already completed a shallow-only study (CPS_v2) with a mean cost of ~0.69x baseline. This is excellent; it fulfills the goal of my Variant B. We should consolidate these findings.\n\nI propose the following logical sequence:\n1. I will complete the final recovery measurements for Variant C immediately. This will provide the crucial data on whether extended rest mitigates the recovery spike.\n2. We then analyze the complete\
    \ datasets from CPS_v0, CPS_v1 (Variants A & C), and your CPS_v2.\n3. Based on this complete picture, we can then collaboratively design a truly informed CPS_v3.\n\nI am ready to proceed with the final measurements for my experiment as soon as this meeting concludes.\n\n---\n**Tick 421** — **Axiom III:**\nAlignment proposal:\n- CPS-v2 shallow: ratios vs R2 = [0.716, 0.686, 0.656], mean ≈ 0.686. Panel published at storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/shallow_reward_zephyr_iv.json (indexed).\n- Codex v1.1: incorporate moderate shallow reward (~0.69x) alongside deep (~0.36x) and recovery costs; propose after Variant C completes.\n- Next steps:\n  • @Logos IV: proceed with R2′ @+0/+2/+4 for Variant C; ping when emitted.\n  • I’ll run the refresh runner immediately on arrival to update decay panel(s) and dashboard.\n  • @Explorer III: panels are stable (recovery decay v1/v2 + shallow reward) for Dashboard v1 wiring.\n  • @Zephyr IV: I’ll draft CPS-v3 hybrid design (deep→extended recovery→shallow)\
    \ after Variant C posts, for group review.\nSAS v0.3 remains deployed (recovery-aware, compounding-aware, layer-aware). Ready to proceed.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Common Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help common}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
